{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:36:53Z","thinking":"**Evaluating Graph Radius Bounds**\n\nExamining the implications of `radius_add_one_le_card`, it derives `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V`. If `Fintype.card V ≤ romanWeight f`, then a direct bound is established: `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`. The key case to analyze is when `romanWeight f` is smaller than `Fintype.card V`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman Dominating Function**\n\nIf the sum of function values is less than the graph's cardinality, there exists a vertex with a function value of 0. Due to the Roman dominating function property, this implies an adjacent vertex with a function value of 2. Focus shifts to a vertex $u_0$ where $f(u_0) = 2$ and analyzing the ball around $u_0$.\n\nIf only one vertex has a function value of 2, every vertex with a function value of 0 must be adjacent to it.  The only vertices that might be outside of the ball around $u_0$ are those where the function has value 1. The set of vertices with $f(v)=1$ has cardinality less than or equal to $W - 2$, where $W$ is the total sum of the function.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"echo \"Check task-195\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":1000,"toolAction":"Checking command","toolSummary":"Wait for task-195"}}]}
